data.content:
The `Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi` 10.0 package upgraded from **OpenAPI.NET v1 to v2** (`Microsoft.OpenApi 2.x`). This is a major breaking change in the underlying library. Here's what changed and how to fix each issue:

---

## 1. `OpenApiAny` types removed

`OpenApiString`, `OpenApiInteger`, etc. are gone. Use native `JsonNode` instead.

```csharp
// Before
param.Schema.Example = new OpenApiString("1.0");

// After
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
```

---

## 2. `OpenApiResponse` → use string descriptions directly

`OpenApiResponse` still exists but `operation.Responses` is now `IDictionary<string, OpenApiResponse>` (unchanged in shape, but verify your import). This part likely still compiles — if not, ensure you're using `Microsoft.OpenApi.Models`.

---

## 3. `OpenApiReference` / `ReferenceType` changes

`ReferenceType` enum is replaced with a string-based `ReferenceType` in v2:

```csharp
// Before
Reference = new OpenApiReference { Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme, Id = "oauth2" }

// After
Reference = new OpenApiReference { Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme, Id = "oauth2" }
// ReferenceType.SecurityScheme still exists but is now a static string constant.
// If it doesn't compile, use:
Reference = new OpenApiReference { Id = "oauth2" }
```

In OpenAPI.NET v2, `OpenApiSecurityScheme` used inside a security requirement only needs the `Id` on the reference — the `Type` is inferred.

---

## 4. `schema.Nullable` removed

OpenAPI v3.1 (which v2 of the library targets) dropped `nullable` in favor of `type` arrays. Use the `Type` property with `JsonSchemaType`:

```csharp
// Before
property.Value.Nullable = false;

// After
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;
property.Value.Type = property.Value.Type & ~JsonSchemaType.Null; // remove Null from flags
```

To **set** nullable: `property.Value.Type |= JsonSchemaType.Null;`

---

## 5. `schema.Required` is now `ISet<string>` → `HashSet<string>`

The `Contains` call should still work, but if `Required` is null, initialize it:

```csharp
schema.Required ??= new HashSet<string>();
```

---

## Fixed code

```csharp
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;

options.AddOperationTransformer((operation, context, ct) =>
{
    var param = operation.Parameters.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Name == "api-version");
    if (param is not null)
    {
        param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
    }

    operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });

    var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecurityScheme
    {
        Reference = new OpenApiReference { Id = "oauth2" }
    };
    operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
    {
        new() { [oAuthScheme] = scopes }
    };

    return Task.CompletedTask;
});

options.AddSchemaTransformer((schema, context, ct) =>
{
    if (schema.Properties is not null)
    {
        foreach (var property in schema.Properties)
        {
            if (schema.Required?.Contains(property.Key) != true)
                property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
        }
    }
    return Task.CompletedTask;
});
```

**Summary of removals:** `Microsoft.OpenApi.Any` namespace is gone (use `System.Text.Json.Nodes`), `Nullable` property is gone (use `JsonSchemaType` flags), and `ReferenceType` on references is now optional/inferred.
